SUMMARY:The Neon Room at Helium: LizaBanks Campagna
LOCATION:Helium Comedy Club\, 1510 SE 9th Ave\, Portland
DESCRIPTION:LizaBanks Campagna is building an entirely new lane in the crea
 tor economy\, one where comedy\, culture\, and civic curiosity collide. In 
 2025\, she emerged as one of the most original voices reshaping how audienc
 es engage with cities\, institutions\, and public life\, proving that educa
 tion and entertainment do not just coexist\, they thrive together.\n\nA sta
 nd-up comedian\, LizaBanks has applied her comedic instincts to an unexpect
 ed arena\, tourism and cultural education. As a New York City tour guide le
 ading sold out experiences at The Metropolitan Museum of Art and Grand Cent
 ral Terminal\, she has transformed traditional sightseeing into immersive\,
  personality driven storytelling. Her tours feel less like lectures and mor
 e like live performances\, attracting audiences who may never have stepped 
 inside a museum otherwise. In the process\, she is modernizing tourism for 
 a social first generation and demonstrating how creators can bring legacy i
 nstitutions into the digital age.\n\nOnline\, LizaBanks extends that same s
 ensibility through content that blends humor\, historical context\, and sha
 rp social observation. In 2025\, she expanded her platform into civic conve
 rsation\, interviewing political figures including Zohran Mamdani and engag
 ing audiences around issues like public transit and accessibility with clar
 ity and curiosity. She frequently collaborates with Overheard\, including h
 osting its Happy Hour series\, and facilitating red carpet interviews. Last
  year\, LizaBanks was profiled in The Cut and appeared on The Today Show wi
 th Al Roker\, signaling her crossover from digital creator to broader cultu
 ral figure.\n\nCouples Package includes:\n\n- 2 premium seats\n- $90 food &
  beverage credit ($45 per person)\n- Gratuity\n- Ticket Protection\n\nManag
 ement reserves the right to prevent customers from entering the facility wh
 o they deem disruptive or dangerous to other patrons.\nMore info: https://c
 omedyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/the-neon-room-at-helium-lizabanks-campagn
 a-21289/
